00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,060
Listen to a talk on an archaeology podcast.

2
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,185
Man:

3
00:00:06,185 --> 00:00:12,230
Throughout the years, archaeologists have discovered many fascinating artifacts on the Greek island of Crete.

4
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:20,117
One example is the Phaistos disc, an ancient clay artifact that was found in

5
00:00:20,117 --> 00:00:24,030
the ruins of the Minoan palace at Phaistos.

6
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:31,906
The Minoan civilization lasted from about 3100 BCE to 1100 BCE,

7
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:39,180
and we think this artifact was made in the second millennium BCE.

8
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:46,301
It was discovered in 1908 and it features many stamped symbols, 241 to be

9
00:00:46,301 --> 00:00:49,210
exact, in the shape of a spiral.

10
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:56,000
The symbols, they include images of things like animals, tools, and so on.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,628
These animals, tools,

12
00:00:57,628 --> 00:01:02,050
and other images form a pattern in the shape of a spiral.

13
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:08,277
What's so interesting is that these symbols are unlike anything else from the Minoan civilization

14
00:01:08,277 --> 00:01:11,110
or any other known writing system.

15
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:15,210
Many experts have tried to decipher these enigmatic symbols.

16
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:19,260
Some suggest they could represent an unknown language.

17
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:26,271
Others think they might represent a calendar or even a religious hymn, yet no

18
00:01:26,271 --> 00:01:28,180
consensus has been reached.

19
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:35,210
Another intriguing thing about the Phaistos disc is the method used to imprint the symbols.

20
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:41,170
This involved pressing prefabricated stamps into wet clay.

21
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,070
This process is really remarkable.

22
00:01:44,070 --> 00:01:49,110
It suggests a level of sophistication similar to early printing.

23
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:55,594
Some scholars hypothesize that the disc might be an import from another culture, a

24
00:01:55,594 --> 00:02:00,090
lone artifact brought to Crete by traders or travelers.

25
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:08,130
But this is another point of contention surrounding this fascinating artifact.
